 1 to 10 km per pixel. Gray grid marks documented no-data and its resampled boundary. Photographed terrain shading remains; globe lighting is approximate.","title":"Global image mosaic","summary":"Source detail ranges from 1 to 10 km per pixel. Photographed shadows remain; the gray grid marks missing imagery."},{"id":"enhanced","label":"Enhanced color","detail":"Color mosaic","thumbnailUrl":"/scenes/io/io-enhanced-thumbnail.webp","description":"USGS enhanced-color mosaic: near-infrared, green and violet color ratios combined with observed monochrome detail. USGS corrected broad limb darkening and matched image seams. Source color detail varies from 1.3 to 21 km per pixel. Interpolated polar color is withheld; observed monochrome remains where available. Gray grid marks missing imagery. Acquisition shading, seams and changes between mission dates can remain; globe lighting is approximate.","title":"False-color mosaic","summary":"Infrared, green and violet ratios add color to monochrome detail. Interpolated polar color is withheld from this view."},{"id":"geology","label":"Geology","detail":"Interpreted units","thumbnailUrl":"/scenes/io/io-geology-thumbnail.webp","description":"Fourteen base geologic units mapped from Voyager and Galileo observations. Colors distinguish interpreted plains, lava flows, patera floors and mountains. The separate diffuse-deposit overlay and structural linework are not shown. Gray grid marks unmapped or conflicting polygons; this view adds no measured relief.","facts":[{"id":"classification","label":"Quantity","value":"Interpreted geologic category"},{"id":"mapping-scale","label":"Map scale","value":"1:15,000,000"},{"id":"epoch","label":"Publication","value":"USGS SIM3168 · 2011"},{"id":"coverage","label":"Coverage","value":"Base-unit polygons; polar/no-data gaps retained"}],"legend":{"kind":"categories","title":"Geologic units","items":[{"label":"Pby","description":"Bright plains","color":"rgb(239 217 105)"},{"label":"Pbw","description":"